{{also|lika|līķa|Lika}}
==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/liːka/}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|líka}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*līkāną}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|líkaði|líkað}}

# to [[please]] {{+obj|is|dat<someone> + nom<someone/something that is pleasing>}} {{q|idiomatically translated by "like" with the grammatical subject and object reversed}}
#: {{ux|is|Mér '''líkar''' góður matur.|I '''like''' good food.}}
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} to [[please]] {{+obj|is|dat<someone> + :við(acc)<someone/something that is pleasing>}} {{q|idiomatically translated by "like" with the dative object as the subject}}
#: {{ux|is|Mér '''líkar''' við þig.|I '''like''' you.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Now used most often in the impersonal construction, using the preposition {{m|is|við}} (see {{m|is|líka við}}).

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|líka við}}
* {{l|is|líka vel við}}
* {{l|is|líka illa við}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|hafa áhuga á}}

===Etymology 2===
See {{m|is|líkur}}.

